  "title": "Joan K NDE 7888",
  "date": "1993",
  "content": "All of the sudden, I was above everything. The first thing I noticed was an amazing feeling of peace, as I've never before experienced. All fear, anger, sadness, and negative emotions were gone. I felt amazing. I could see myself and the doctors, nurses, and medical staff. But they were only an observation. I had no feeling or judgment of them, they just were and I just was. Then I looked at myself and I was light. I had the shape of a person, but was only made up of a yellow light. I wasn't scared, just maybe curious. Then I felt I had to go somewhere else, so I began to fly away and upwards. That is all I remember. When I woke up in the recovery room, I decided that it was a dream. Then later on, I asked the nurse why my throat hurt so badly. She said they had to put the tube down my throat because I stopped breathing. I guess it could all have been a dream, but that overwhelming peace is something I have never felt before or again. There is nothing like it.",
